videos-list-*.json (platforms/ytConfirm.test.js) are NOT captured: they are videos.list
(part=snippet,liveStreamingDetails) responses written 2026-10-24 from the Data API's documented
resource shape (developers.google.com/youtube/v3/docs/videos: snippet.liveBroadcastContent
live / upcoming / none; liveStreamingDetails.actualStartTime, actualEndTime, scheduledStartTime,
concurrentViewers, activeLiveChatId), trimmed to the fields the classifier reads. Capturing them needs
an API key and a call against the quota; the first real confirm on a live night should be compared
with them (Task 12). Video id is the tests' placeholder.
videos-list-live.json — a broadcast live now
videos-list-upcoming.json — a scheduled broadcast (scheduledStartTime only)
videos-list-none.json — an ordinary upload, never live (no liveStreamingDetails)
videos-list-ended.json — a finished broadcast (liveBroadcastContent none, actualEndTime set)
videos-list-empty.json — an id that names nothing (deleted or private): no items
